From: IMX6ULL AV Project <learning-project@local>
Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC] media: mx6s-csi: sample parallel PCLK on falling edge

This patch is an A/B diagnostic for the VIDEO-R5 natural-image corruption
seen at VGA 30 fps.  The original NXP 4.1.15 driver sets BIT_REDGE and samples
the parallel CSI bus on the rising PCLK edge.  Clear BIT_REDGE in variant B so
that the receiver samples on the falling edge.

Keep the sensor format, timing and polarity registers unchanged while testing.
This patch is deliberately not the final product configuration: if variant B
is proven better on hardware, a later cleanup will expose the edge selection
as a device-tree property instead of leaving it hard-coded.

The second change keeps the same edge if the driver ever leaves TV-decoder
mode.  VGA progressive capture does not normally execute that path, but
covering it prevents a future mode change from silently restoring REDGE.

---
 drivers/media/platform/mxc/subdev/mx6s_capture.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/mxc/subdev/mx6s_capture.c b/drivers/media/platform/mxc/subdev/mx6s_capture.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/mxc/subdev/mx6s_capture.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mxc/subdev/mx6s_capture.c
@@ -457,7 +457,14 @@ static void csi_init_interface(struct mx6s_csi_dev *csi_dev)
 	unsigned int imag_para;
 
 	val |= BIT_SOF_POL;
-	val |= BIT_REDGE;
+	/*
+	 * VIDEO-R5 PCLK edge A/B test, variant B:
+	 *
+	 * BIT_REDGE=1 selects rising-edge sampling.  Keep it cleared here so
+	 * the CSI receiver samples the OV5640 parallel bus on the falling edge.
+	 * Do not change OV5640 timing/polarity registers during this test.
+	 */
+	val &= ~BIT_REDGE;
 	val |= BIT_GCLK_MODE;
 	val |= BIT_HSYNC_POL;
 	val |= BIT_FCC;
@@ -555,6 +562,8 @@ static void csi_tvdec_enable(struct mx6s_csi_dev *csi_dev, bool enable)
 				BIT_BASEADDR_CHG_ERR_EN);
 		cr1 &= ~BIT_CCIR_MODE;
-		cr1 |= BIT_SOF_POL | BIT_REDGE;
+		cr1 |= BIT_SOF_POL;
+		/* Preserve VIDEO-R5 variant B after leaving TV-decoder mode. */
+		cr1 &= ~BIT_REDGE;
 	}
 
 	__raw_writel(cr18, csi_dev->regbase + CSI_CSICR18);
@@ -1172,6 +1181,8 @@ static int mx6s_csi_open(struct file *file)
 
 	v4l2_subdev_call(sd, core, s_power, 1);
 	mx6s_csi_init(csi_dev);
+	dev_info(csi_dev->dev,
+		 "VIDEO-R5 A/B: parallel PCLK sampling edge = falling\n");
 
 	mutex_unlock(&csi_dev->lock);
 
-- 
